6001	    /// Always-defer invariant (codex finding 1/2): even with NO tentative window
6002	    /// live, a global-request handler NEVER pushes or pops the run queue
6003	    /// directly -- both admission and removal are buffered and take effect only
6004	    /// at the deterministic step2 drain. This removes the host-timing-dependent
6005	    /// immediate path: whichever daemon phase a handler happened to race, it only
6006	    /// records intent, so the run-queue mutation is applied at one fixed point in
6007	    /// DetTid order regardless of host arrival timing.
6008	    #[test]
6009	    fn run_queue_mutations_always_defer_to_the_drain() {
